Package: com.huhansibuxin.cachedeletequiet
Name: CacheDeleteQuiet
Version: 1.3.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: PLAN D4: kills the 80-99% CPU spikes of CacheDeleteAppContainerCaches by rebinding, inside that one XPC helper process, the arm64e auth-GOT slots of the recursive C scans (_fast_size_directory / _traverse_directory). v1.3.0 FIXES THE v1.2.0 CRASH LOOP: two IPS (00:12:06 / 00:15:53) proved EXC_BAD_ACCESS SIGSEGV "possible pointer authentication failure" on the purgeable queue, because the saved original was a ptrauth_strip()ped pointer while arm64e function-pointer calls compile to `blraaz x8` (IA key, zero modifier) - a stripped pointer fails that authentication and the branch target becomes garbage. v1.3.0 stores ptrauth_sign_unauthenticated(stripped, IA, 0), proves the re-auth round trip numerically, rejects any slot that points at our own wrappers, adds a 4-starts-per-5-minutes crash breaker that permanently downgrades to orig-free skips, and adds per-API kill switches (SKIP_ITEMIZED / SKIP_ENUM / SKIP_PERSONAS / SKIP_LARGEAPP / SKIP_RECENTAPP). Flags in /var/mobile/Documents/CacheDeleteQuiet/ (or /var/tmp): PROBE_ONLY (rebind but call original, A/B baseline), PASSTHROUGH_ALL (no rebind), STRICT, DISABLED, plus the v1.3.0 per-API switches SKIP_ITEMIZED / SKIP_ENUM / SKIP_PERSONAS / SKIP_LARGEAPP / SKIP_RECENTAPP; touch then kickstart -k. No substrate/ellekit/Foundation link, no Logos, no timers, no polling.  Log: /var/tmp/CacheDeleteQuiet.log (SSH: /rootfs/private/var/tmp/CacheDeleteQuiet.log).
Maintainer: huhansibuxin
Author: huhansibuxin
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit
